---
source: cli/tests/help.rs
expression: text
---
Send the subvolume(s) to stdout.

Generate a stream representation of one or more subvolumes that can be
transmitted over the network or stored for later restoration. A stream can be
incremental, based on a parent subvolume, to only send changes. The stream is in
btrfs send format and can be received with the receive command. Requires
CAP_SYS_ADMIN.

With --offline, the kernel BTRFS_IOC_SEND ioctl is bypassed and the stream is
generated by reading the image directly. This works for images that aren't
mounted, for FUSE mounts where the ioctl can't complete, and without privileges
(CAP_SYS_ADMIN is not required). Offline mode only does full sends. Incremental
sends, clone sources, NO_FILE_DATA, other protocol versions, and compressed-data
passthrough are not yet supported there.

Usage: send [OPTIONS] [SUBVOLUMES]...

Arguments:
  [SUBVOLUMES]...
          Subvolume(s) to send. Required unless --offline is given

Options:
  -e, --omit-end-cmd
          Omit end-cmd marker between subvolumes

  -f, --outfile <OUTFILE>
          Write output to a file instead of stdout

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Incremental:
  -p, --parent <PARENT>
          Send an incremental stream from parent to the subvolume

  -c, --clone-src <CLONE_SRC>
          Use this snapshot as a clone source (may be given multiple times)

Protocol:
      --no-data
          Send in NO_FILE_DATA mode

      --proto <PROTO>
          Use send protocol version N (0 means the highest the kernel supports)

      --compressed-data
          Send compressed data directly without decompressing

Offline mode:
      --offline <IMAGE>
          Unmounted btrfs image or block device to send from
          
          Bypasses the kernel ioctl and requires no privileges.

      --offline-subvol <OFFLINE_SUBVOL>
          Path of the subvolume to send in --offline mode
          
          The path is slash-separated and relative to the filesystem root.
          Defaults to the default subvolume (FS_TREE) when neither this nor
          --offline-subvolid is set.

      --offline-subvolid <OFFLINE_SUBVOLID>
          Tree id of the subvolume to send in --offline mode
          
          Mutually exclusive with --offline-subvol.
